Well everyone else was complaining that it was *SO* easy to win with a Priest
due to the wraiths in the Quest. So I played one.

Teflon the Priest was pretty good- 18/50 or so STR, 18 in everything else
except INT, which was about 13 (lots of blessed potions of gain ability).
He was 30th level w/ 500 hps and the +5 Excalibur. All necessary intrinsics
except magic and disintigration resistance. No reflection. AC -7.

I had cleaned everything else out and figured I was ready for Nalzok (or
whoever the big nasty Quest monster is). I almost killed him but he teleported
to the up staircase and fled upstairs. I chased him up only to have him
teleport away to heal. When I reached him he duplicated, destroyed my elven
cloak and +3 speed boots and mauled me. *I* fled up the staircase (which I
was standing on to keep him from doing the same) and he followed me, duplicating
again in the process. I died.

Nalzok IS a big nasty monster and you NEED all those hp's to have a chance.
He duplicates, destroys armor, and does 20-30 hps of damage per hit, 3 hits.

In the future I plan to go to the castle first to get my wishes and a *MUCH*
lower AC (for those who don't know, below -8 AC it reduces damage done to you,
not their chance to hit).

Is there anything else I could've done to live? The armor destroying is
particularly deadly- would disintigration resist. have stopped this?
